# kpp's output: a C* thrown is no match for a handler of B*& ([except.handle] 3: only cv T and const T& take the conversion), so B* const& catches it; clang's MSVC target crashes (0xC0000005) and llvm-mingw's catches it by B*& (Itanium's runtime matches it, a known bug).
B* const& 2 1 | 2
B* const& -1 0 | 2
B* const& -1 0 | 2
const void* 0 | 4
const void* 1 | 4
exact B*& 2 | 1
any | 5
const A* 1 | 1
const A* -1 | 1
const A* -1 | 1
exit 0
